  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Addressing the most urgent shelter needs of vulnerable people affected by hurricane Melissa in Jamaica</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">IOM is launching an emergency response project in Jamaica following the catastrophic impact of Hurricane Melissa, a Category 5 storm that struck in October 2025. This project aims to rapidly restore dignified living conditions for people whose homes were severely damaged in the parishes of Hanover, Westmoreland, Trelawny, and St. James. IOM is mobilizing and distributing essential Non-Food Items (NFIs) and immediate shelter repair kits, such as tarpaulins and basic tools, to vulnerable households. The intervention is rooted in protection principles, ensuring strong community engagement, the inclusion of vulnerable groups, and the mitigation of risks like Gender-Based Violence (GBV). This life-saving assistance contributes to ongoing efforts to ensure affected families can quickly begin rebuilding their lives safely.</narrative>
  </description>
